        "snippetId": "s573",
        "messageOrdinal": 21,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-05-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 May 1845",
        "text": "May I ask how the head is? just under the bag?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s601",
        "messageOrdinal": 24,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-05-16",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "16 May 1845",
        "text": "Only not mistrustful.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s1180",
        "messageOrdinal": 78,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-08-13",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "13 August 1845",
        "text": "Yes, I admit that it was stupid to read that word so wrong.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s1301",
        "messageOrdinal": 86,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-08-25",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "25 August 1845",
        "text": "I asked no question from the moment when my last hope went: and since then, it has been impossible for me to speak what was in me.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s3034",
        "messageOrdinal": 181,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-12-24",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "24 December 1845",
        "text": "Yet even when I grow too wise, I admit always that while you love me it is an answer to all.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s3129",
        "messageOrdinal": 184,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-12-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 December 1845",
        "text": "The whole breaking round him of the cloud, and the manner in which he stands, facing it, ...",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6075",
        "messageOrdinal": 310,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-13",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "13 April 1846",
        "text": "And all this reminds me of what I have often and often mused about saying to you, and shrank back, and torn the paper now and then....",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6504",
        "messageOrdinal": 327,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-04-24",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "24 April 1846",
        "text": "I thank God for that, first of all.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6648",
        "messageOrdinal": 333,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-04-28",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "28 April 1846",
        "text": "One letter more I get, do I not?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s8142",
        "messageOrdinal": 402,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-06-13",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "13 June 1846",
        "text": "In the meanwhile, I should laugh to scorn all that sort of calumny ... even if I could believe it to be possible.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
}
